      "text": "Cusco to Lima"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a8704e80dc128a8",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "debc694eafa0915b55137540f364fce450dd9f854af319c828c1566aaf345205",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-97d3eeec2bfb-mw9olsy5",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, visit archaeological sites around Cusco.\n\nAt Sacsayhuamán, a site sacred to the Incas, you’ll see the massive stonework. You’ll also learn about Qorikancha, the Temple of the Sun, which was associated with gold ornamentation in Inca times. After the Spanish arrived, a monastery was built on the site. An earthquake later damaged parts of the colonial building, exposing the Inca stone walls beneath it.\n\nContinue to Tambomachay, a water temple with channels and pools, and to Puka Pukara, the Red Fortress, which served as a guard post.\n\nAfter the tour, transfer to the airport for your flight to Lima. On arrival, transfer to your hotel.\n\nThe morning brings together several key sites around Cusco. Sacsayhuamán is known for its huge stone blocks, Qorikancha for its association with sun worship, Tambomachay for its water and channels, and Puka Pukara for its defensive role. Before flying to Lima, you’ll have time to explore how Inca architecture reflected religious beliefs."
    },
